@title Kessakusen! Ganbare Goemon 1+2 - Yuki-hime to Magginesu (Japan)
@file Kessakusen Ganbare! Goemon 1 and 2 (J).gba
@game BG2J
@chip EEPROM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@save skip: nothing reaches the EEPROM through Goemon 2's whole first stage, the area map, Satsuma village (the old man, the Oedo Tourist teleport desk, the meshiya) or a game over given up with まいった; the diary (たびにっき) slots fill later in the game, and enemy hits and town NPCs come out different on each emulator (see below), so no frozen walk reaches it
# The cart holds both SNES games. Goemon 2 (マッギネスをあそぶ): たびにっき 1
# はじめから, ゴエモン, START past the intro, Area 1: the beach stage on foot
# (B pipe, A jump), the fish mech (hit it, jump on: B shoots, A flies) over
# the water to the tanuki statue, whose coins end the stage. The map
# (りゅうきゅう りぞーと, 175両 on all three), up to さつま むら: the old man's
# house (dialogue), the 旅 shop (大江戸ツーリスト さつまむら支店, a teleport
# service at 50両; いいえ).
# Goemon 1 (ゆきひめをあそぶ) was tried first and left: its overhead town has
# enemies that walk differently on each emulator within the first half
# minute of play (mgba's samurai at f3328, then nba's ghost from f5300 and
# all three apart by f5868), and its diary keeper is only met past stage 1.
# Findings while authoring Goemon 2:
# - nba runs the player's animations a frame or two behind the other two
#   (attack swings, f4240 on), and its camera trails vertically by a few
#   pixels during jumps (f4314, f9330); the game outcome stays the same.
# - f6544, riding the fish over the water: dingbat-bios and nba kill the
#   bunny that jumps out at the right edge with the first shot, mgba's shot
#   misses it and it lands (explosions differ from then until f6580). The
#   route here waits for the bunny to land and shoots it point blank, which
#   all three agree on.
# - The じかん timer ticks a unit earlier on mgba (f6748: 67 on mgba, 68 on
#   the others; Goemon 1 the same at f4175), so mgba runs a logic frame
#   ahead somewhere: the game drops frames on load.
# - Translucent text boxes blend one 5-bit step apart: dingbat-bios one step
#   darker than both references where they agree (Goemon 1's kuchiire-ya
#   box, 2683 pixels, stable for 130 frames), the 5-bit alpha rounding the
#   SP photographs gave (docs/hwprobe-questions.md; Trick Star's script has
#   the arithmetic). mgba and nba also differ from each other by a step in
#   places (the player-select portrait, the beach stage's last scanline).
# - Town villagers walk differently on all three (Satsuma, f7810 mgba, then
#   f11240 all three); harmless here.
# - The blank EEPROM comes out 512 bytes on mgba and 8192 on nba.
# In the replay all four dingbat configurations draw what mgba draws up to
# first_gameplay; nba is a frame behind there (area_card, first_gameplay
# SLIP +1) and its player_select portrait blends differently; the map is
# MINOR between all three, old_man a frame apart each way; tourist identical.

